WEBVTT

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.530
What do you mean you can't use this plan?

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.660
Lucius,

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.490
let me be honest with you.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.910
Your idea is outdated.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.960
W-What?!

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.710
Don't you get it?

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.420
These days Rome is looking for innovation.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.460
A-And that's what I'm trying to achieve

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.380
by showing our society the style of the good ole days,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.640
which have already been long forgotten.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.550
Lucius...

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.270
Just take a look at Rome.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.560
Ever since Hadrian became the Emperor,

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.230
innovative buildings were built one after another.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:53.440
The Emperor himself is a great architect who reconstructed the Greek Acropolis.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.110
Listen, Lucius...

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.330
If you build something reckless that does not fit in this era, it could cost you your life.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Re-Reckless, you say?!

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.340
I have traveled as far as Athens in order to learn the greatest techniques in architecture!

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.130
And you call my plans reckless?!

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.420
That is not what I mean.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:19.470
What I do mean, however, is that I cannot adopt your plans.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.890
You will regret losing me.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.880
Oh well, Lucius.

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:52.880
Don't dwell on that.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:58.430
No. This trade wants no more of me, Marcus.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:04.890
Don't say that. Just take a good hot bath like this, and something will come to you.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.570
Snacks! Anyone wants snacks?

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.820
Delicious snacks, anyone?

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.780
Epilation!

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.360
Your armpits will shine with cleanliness!

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.280
But don't you think this bath is a bit too noisy, Marcus?

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.200
Oh, I think I'll get epilated today!

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.580
Here, hey!

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.210
I want to get epilated!

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:29.420
Thank you!

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.790
The bath is meant to be a place for relaxing.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:42.300
It's simply crazy that I have to go
underwater to get any peace and quiet.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:43.720
Huh?

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.390
That's one strange drain.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.140
How does it work?

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.770
Where is this suction coming from?!

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.910
Ah, a light...

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.410
Is that the exit?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.870
A light!

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.140
W-Where...

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.610
am I?!

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.570
Is that not... Mount Vesuvius of Pompeii?

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:50.790
Hey, you! Have you been down there this whole time?

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.750
I didn't notice you at all!

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.080
And they aren't Romans!

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.000
Their faces are flat!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:01.170
I see. This is probably a bath for the slaves,

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.430
and I accidentally ended up here.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:08.260
It seems he doesn't understand what you're saying.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.730
That's a shame. I wonder if he's alone.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:16.730
I see. So water from that bath drains

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.320
into this one for the flat-faced slaves.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.070
You know, you're pretty red from the heat. You should take a break outside.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.990
Does he mean this isn't a bath for Romans?

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.370
Got it? Outside. Break.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.910
Well, I can understand it.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.750
This might be the only place the slaves can relax.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:42.630
On the other hand, this place shows signs of advanced culture.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.930
I've never even seen this material before.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.390
Just look at this beautiful golden pigment!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.020
You've never seen one before? Where are you from anyway?

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.600
Why is he laughing at me?

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.940
Is he insinuating that the world famed Romans

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:01.690
don't know how to make something like this?

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:08.490
Y'know, the boss here is my old friend, so feel free to take it if you want.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.330
How dare a lowly slave make fun of a Roman!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.630
Hey! I just can't stand this heat.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.050
Hey, Sada. Welcome.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:36.140
What a huge mirror! It's so big!

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:40.400
And the perfection of these event advertisements!

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:44.320
Hey, you look a bit like Abe Hiroshi!

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.660
What is this?

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:54.660
A soothing wind is cooling my body.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:02.000
And why am I saying "aah"?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.470
I can make use of this slave bath!

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:10.930
From the current baths that focus only on size and luxury,

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.220
this is a return to simplicity and multifunctionality.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.600
You... can't find your clothes?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:22.570
They have a beautiful painting of Mount Vesuvius in the bath,

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:26.990
and a giant mirror and event advertisements in the changing room.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:31.030
Isn't this exactly what Rome is looking for in its search for innovation?

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:36.410
Although, why do these people possess such advanced techniques?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:42.250
Everything that I have learned during my years of travel to Athens pales in comparison to this!

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.760
Are you feeling sick?

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:50.760
I understand completely now. These flat-faced people possess advanced technology

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.350
and value bath culture more than anyone I know.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:07:02.350
However, I need to inform them that because they became part of Rome,

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.650
we Romans have the right to assimilate their culture.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.780
Hey.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.070
Look, a fruit drink.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:14.280
After a nice bath, you should drink this.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.660
Here, I opened it for you.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:22.500
It'll refresh you.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.340
What? Is he telling me to drink this?

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.090
I <i>am</i> really thirsty.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:33.840
Anyway, if it will quench my thirst...

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:44.270
T-This is...

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:51.070
fabulous!

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.910
It's cold and sweet!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:58.160
It tastes like cow milk mixed with fruits from the warm South.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.950
And it's cold like snow at the same time.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:03.420
This soft taste that cools the fire of the bath in my body...

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.210
Is it really of this world?!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.590
See, he likes it.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.550
This sweetness is like a dream.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.970
Wanna have another one?

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:23.560
Huh?

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.980
Lucius! Hey, Lucius!

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:33.610
What? Where is that flat-faced slave?

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.530
What are you talking about?!

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:38.780
You almost drowned in the pool!

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.120
Was it all a dream then?

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:51.710
A dream, yet not a dream!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.100
Hey, have you heard about it?

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.180
What?

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.270
The new bath that opened nearby!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:06.310
The one that has Vesuvius painted on its wall?

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:11.820
They say the drinks there are out of this world.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:13.860
Then let's check it out next time.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:22.490
So I should put my clothes in here?

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:27.040
A guard slave is watching over them, so you needn't worry.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.170
I saw this comedy last week!

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.590
I wanted to go see it as well.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.340
This is so elegant!

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:44.310
If you have Vesuvius, then the Gulf of Naples and pine trees are a must.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.520
Line up here, please!

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:53.610
Have a cow milk drink with fruit juice in it!

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.070
Please don't take more than one!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:59.700
This is amazing, Lucius.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.830
Just a little while ago, you were unemployed and depressed,

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.830
and look at you now! You're a popular architect!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.000
What on earth happened?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.460
Lord Lucius!

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:13.090
We need to buy another cow or we won't have enough milk!

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.550
I see. Get it done.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.720
This is really amazing!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:24.180
Sorry, Marcus, but I don't understand most of this myself.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:29.520
For example, the bottles made in that world are frighteningly perfect.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:33.820
This is better than what even skilled Roman professionals can do!

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:41.660
You know, Lucius, if you cooled this a bit more, it would be even better.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:45.740
We're already cooling it as much as possible using underground water.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:52.540
How was the drink in that world so cold?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:57.300
We're even using corks to prevent the contents from spilling while being carried,

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.800
but that's making them harder to open rather than easier.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:07.100
What did that flat-faced man use to open it so easily?

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:12.020
Also, no matter how hard I searched for that bath of flat-faced slaves,

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.610
I couldn't find it anywhere.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:18.440
Do I have no way of returning there to learn more?

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:25.200
By the way, Lucius, remember that bath where you almost drowned?

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.870
Seems like they found some huge hole in it,

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:32.210
and they're going to demolish it because it's dangerous.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:34.920
I can't let that happen!

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.000
H-Hey!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.510
Where are you going, Lucius?!

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:43.970
I-I must at least learn how they opened the bottle!
